# No rewrite rules, on purpose.
#
# Every page worth a search result is prerendered to its own HTML file by
# scripts/prerender.ts (products sold by 2+ shops, categories, departments,
# shelves, static pages). Cloudflare Pages applies _redirects BEFORE static
# files, so the old `/prices/*  /  200` style rules would have served the
# homepage in place of every prerendered page. Measured in `wrangler pages dev`.
#
# Anything not prerendered (single-shop products, typos) gets dist/404.html,
# which prerender.ts writes as the app shell: the app boots at the requested
# URL and renders the page or its own "not found", with a 404 status.
#
# ⛔ Never point a rule at /index.html (Pages strips .html and loops), and
# never add a `/*` catch-all.
